{
  "info": {
    "name": "revDSM — Installer Module",
    "description": "Installer endpoints for the revDSM mobile app.\n\nUsage:\n1. Set the `base_url` collection variable (default: https://demo-api.revdsm.com).\n2. Run **Auth > Login** — the test script stores `token` automatically.\n3. Run **My Jobs**, copy a job `_id` into the `job_id` variable (or the list request's test script grabs the first one for you).\n4. **Update Job Status** with `{ \"status\": \"inProgress\" }` returns the full working payload (contractDetails + preInstallPhotos + productDetails).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{token}}", "type": "string" }]
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "https://demo-api.revdsm.com", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "token", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "job_id", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "email", "value": "revdsminc@gmail.com", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "password", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "const token = res?.data?.accessToken || res?.accessToken || res?.data?.token || res?.token;",
                  "if (token) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', token);",
                  "  console.log('Saved token');",
                  "} else {",
                  "  console.warn('No token found in login response — set `token` manually.');",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('Login OK', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 201]));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\",\n  \"deviceId\": \"postman\",\n  \"trustDevice\": true\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/company/login",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["company", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Custom JWT bearer login. Captures `accessToken` into the `token` variable via the test script."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Me (profile)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/company",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["company"]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Installer",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "My Jobs",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "const payload = res?.data ?? res ?? {};",
                  "const rows = Array.isArray(payload) ? payload : (payload.jobs || []);",
                  "if (rows.length && rows[0]?._id) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('job_id', rows[0]._id);",
                  "  console.log('job_id set to', rows[0]._id);",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/installer/v1/my-jobs?period=all",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["installer", "v1", "my-jobs"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "period", "value": "all", "description": "all | future" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Jobs assigned to the signed-in installer. `period=all` backs the \"All\" tab, `period=future` backs \"Upcoming\" (preview-only — those jobs open read-only). Response: `{ data: { jobs[], pagination, summaryCounts } }`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Job Status (start / result)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"inProgress\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/installer/v1/update/{{job_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["installer", "v1", "update", "{{job_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "Moves a job through the workflow. Replaces the retired `PUT /installer/v1/update-job-status/:id`.\n\nSAME PATH as the step-data save, DIFFERENT VERB: PUT is a transition and carries nothing but `status` (+ `statusReason`); PATCH carries `stepData`.\n\nWorkflow statuses: `scheduled` | `inProgress` | `completed` | `onHold`.\nResult statuses (wire codes, not the button labels):\n  { \"status\": \"cantDoWork\", \"statusReason\": \"Site unsafe\" }\n  { \"status\": \"notHit\", \"statusReason\": \"Customer was not home\" }\n\nReset is NOT a status — see `PUT /installer/v1/:id/reset`.\n\nThe full working payload — `contractDetails`, `preInstallPhotos`, `productDetails` — comes from the check-in call (`PUT /installer/v1/:id/work`), not from here."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Reset Job",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"statusReason\": \"Manager reopened job for crew follow-up\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/installer/v1/{{job_id}}/reset",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["installer", "v1", "{{job_id}}", "reset"]
            },
            "description": "Reopens a resulted job so the crew can come back to it. The reason travels as `statusReason` (NOT `reason`).\n\nResponds with a summary — `{ _id, leadId, jobNumber, previousStatus, status }` — not the job. The server decides what the job returns to (`inProgress`).\n\nThe app follows a successful reset with a PATCH to `/installer/v1/update/:id` that clears every step's data."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Job",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/installer/v1/jobs/{{job_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["installer", "v1", "jobs", "{{job_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "Single job detail. (Provisional — confirm before use; mobile currently mocks this.)"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Save Progress",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"completedSteps\": {\n    \"pre\": true\n  },\n  \"updatedAt\": \"2026-07-23T09:00:00.000Z\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/installer/v1/jobs/{{job_id}}/progress",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["installer", "v1", "jobs", "{{job_id}}", "progress"]
            },
            "description": "Persists per-job install timeline progress. (Provisional.)"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Submit Result",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"result\": \"Can't Do Work\",\n  \"reason\": \"Access blocked — customer not home\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/installer/v1/jobs/{{job_id}}/result",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["installer", "v1", "jobs", "{{job_id}}", "result"]
            },
            "description": "Result types: `Can't Do Work` | `Reset` | `Not Hit`. (Provisional.)"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Report Discrepancy",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"productId\": \"6a28fa6ed6700f1190253ad2__6a34e97e39e195278cd47945\",\n  \"issue\": \"Footage mismatch\",\n  \"note\": \"Sold 40ft, site measures 52ft\",\n  \"attachments\": []\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/installer/v1/jobs/{{job_id}}/discrepancy",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["installer", "v1", "jobs", "{{job_id}}", "discrepancy"]
            },
            "description": "Routes a scope discrepancy to the Install Manager and originating rep. (Provisional.)"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
